  "reconstructibility": 1,
  "reason": "The records collectively point toward Cr alloying of BCC refractory HEAs, Cr-rich multicomponent Laves-phase formation, lattice-distortion strengthening, and microstructural topology as a way to balance strength and ductility. In particular, R6-R8 disclose Cr-containing BCC refractory alloys with Cr-rich Laves phases, R13 shows a Laves phase in a closely related Hf-Nb-Ti-V-Zr system, and R2/R14 provide the lattice-distortion mechanism. R12 further suggests that controlling whether an intermetallic phase is continuous or dispersed can preserve ductility. However, none discloses dilute Cr addition to HfMoTaTiZr or identifies a reticulated Laves network as beneficial for crack deflection and plasticity compensation; some instead characterize Laves phases as detrimental. Thus the records suggest the general direction, but the specific beneficial network morphology and its crack-hindrance role require a substantial additional idea."
}
